Palace queens cry where goes our refuge --- Queens praise Rāma angerless consoler of all --- Queens call king senseless for exiling Rāma --- Fire rites cease and sun veils itself --- Elephants cast food and cows withhold milk --- Planets turn cruel and stars lose luster --- Citizens abandon food play and joy --- All Ayōdhyā thinks only of Rāma --- Bereft Ayōdhyā quakes like Indra-less earth
